      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 & -24 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 8 & 9 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -15 \\\\ -10 & 9 & 63\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary column operations of the form $C_i:=C_i+kC_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary column operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{12}=3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 & -24 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 8 & 9 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{1}:=C_{1}-2C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & -24 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ -10 & 9 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\\\ &\\xrightarrow{C_{3}:=C_{3}+8C_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -15 \\\\ -10 & 9 & 63\\end{bmatrix}\\\\ &=B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary column operations are\n\n$C_{1}:=C_{1}-2C_{2}$ and $C_{3}:=C_{3}+8C_{2}$.",
